This project includes, and in places adapts, the Lean formalization

    anthropics/formal-math, directory 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011
    https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/main/3sum-apsp
    Copyright (c) 2026 Anthropic, PBC. Released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

of the paper "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided
Graphs" by Josh Alman and Virginia Vassilevska Williams (arXiv:2610.06783). The algorithms that
this project analyzes and modifies are theirs.

The directory upstream/3sum-apsp contains the 340 Lean files of that formalization that this
project imports, directly or transitively, with its LICENSE and NOTICE, ported from Lean and
Mathlib v4.33.1 to v4.35.0-rc2. Four of the files were changed by the port; each carries in its
header the line "Modified in 2026 for ImprovedExponents (Jihoon Hyun): ported to Lean and Mathlib
v4.35.0-rc2.", and upstream/README.md lists them with the changes. Every other file is
upstream's, unchanged; scripts/check-upstream.sh confirms this against the commit above. The
NOTICE of that formalization (upstream/3sum-apsp/NOTICE) reads:

    ThreeSumApsp: a Lean 4 formalization of "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in
    Sparse Lopsided Graphs"
    Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC

    This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

    The comments of the Lean files and the documents of this product quote statements and sentences of the paper named
    above. The quoted passages are included, under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with the permission of the authors of
    the paper.

    This product depends on, but does not include, Lean 4 (https://github.com/leanprover/lean4) and
    mathlib4 with its standard dependency set, fetched by the build tool from their public repositories at the
    revisions pinned in lake-manifest.json: batteries, aesop, Qq, ProofWidgets4, import-graph, LeanSearchClient and
    plausible are released under the Apache License, Version 2.0; Cli (leanprover/lean4-cli) is released under the
    MIT License (Copyright (c) 2021 mhuisi). None of these dependencies is included in this product, apart from
    four proofs in ThreeSumApsp/Util/PrimesInWindow.lean: the proofs of prod_middle_le and centralBinom_le are adapted
    from that of centralBinom_le_of_no_bertrand_prime, and the proofs of concaveOn_log_add_sqrt_mul_log_sub and
    log_add_sqrt_mul_log_le from that of Bertrand.real_main_inequality, all in the file
    Mathlib/NumberTheory/Bertrand.lean of mathlib4 (Copyright (c) 2020 Patrick Stevens. All rights reserved. Released under
    Apache 2.0 license. Authors: Patrick Stevens, Bolton Bailey).

ImprovedChallenge.lean contains, between the documentation comment "Claims of the paper ..." and
the line "end EndStatement", the file EndStatement.lean of that formalization, copied without any
change (scripts/check-endstatement.sh confirms this against upstream/3sum-apsp/EndStatement.lean,
which is upstream's file, unchanged). Its comments quote statements and sentences of the paper, as
the upstream NOTICE records.

